  "description": "E-MAIL ONLY – Please send an email, including your mobile number, to apply for a viewing of this property. We will respond to applicants in the order in which enquiries are received. Please state how many people the property would be for and provide a brief introduction to each person. We apologise in advance that, due to the high level of interest, we may not be able to respond to everyone.\n\nBrady Property Management are delighted to bring this well-appointed property in the highly sought-after development of Seamount to the market. Located just off the N11, this three-bedroom apartment is presented in great condition, having just being re-decorated and furnished.  The property benefits from a south-west facing balcony with a private aspect overlooking the wooded area in the communal grounds.\n\nThe property is entered through a large spacious hallway and leads into a bright living room, with double doors opening onto the balcony. The kitchen is fitted with a range of units and integrated appliances, with a dining area.\n\nThere are three good-sized bedrooms, with the master bedroom benefiting from built-in wardrobes, a private balcony and an en-suite shower room. The second bedroom is a good-sized double bedroom with built-in wardrobes, while the third bedroom also benefits from built-in storage and can be furnished as a single bedroom, depending on the needs of the resident. There is also a main bathroom with a bath and shower.\n\nThe property comes with one designated parking space. Seamount is a well-maintained development with mature communal gardens and is ideally located close to UCD, Blackrock and Stillorgan. There are a range of shops, cafés, restaurants and other amenities nearby, while Booterstown DART station and the bus services along the N11 provide convenient transport links to Dublin city centre and surrounding areas. The M50 is also within easy reach, making it a convenient location for commuters.\n\nThe property is ideally located for anyone looking to be close to UCD, the city centre, Blackrock and Stillorgan, while still benefiting from a quiet residential development. It is a must-see for anyone looking in the area.\n\nPlease note that, due to environmental and hygiene reasons, we operate a no-mattress policy. Tenants may therefore have to provide their own mattress.",
